  "id": "pseudoneurological",
  "term": "pseudoneurological",
  "definition": "Pseudoneurological describes bodily symptoms that resemble neurological problems but are understood here as somatic expressions of dissociation. In this context, they are linked to disruptions in the normal integration of consciousness, memory, or identity, often in relation to trauma or other psychological stress.",
